#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166599 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/id #uuid "3817c58a-1176-5347-aa96-2846969cae32" :question/math-academy-id "e-8349" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $y = 3\\sech{x}+\\coth{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFirst, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n( \\sech x )' = -\\sech x\\tanh x,\n\\quad \n( \\csch x )' = -\\csch x \\coth x,\n\\quad \n( \\coth x )' = -\\csch^2 x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results and the rules of differentiation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)+(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{csch}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166600 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "b14f0558-456d-51a9-85ac-0b36158bc52e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8350" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) =\\coth(5x - 2).$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFirst, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf =\\coth{g}, \\qquad g = 5x - 2\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}x} = \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g} \\cdot \\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}f} {\\textrm{d}g}  = -\\csch^2{g},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}g} {\\textrm{d}x} = 5.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =-5{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-5{csch}^{2}⁡(5x-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166601 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "4baa8799-f8ce-521e-833b-8b66c747e701" :question/math-academy-id "e-8351" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = x^2\\coth{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nHere, we have the product of two functions $u(x) = x^2$ and $v(x) = \\coth{x}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =x(2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166602 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/id #uuid "bec9b472-31ce-5892-8a17-c4aa3c33ef12" :question/math-academy-id "e-8352" :question/problem "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x) = \\dfrac{\\sech{x}}{4x}.$" :question/worked-solution "$\\newcommand{\\arsinh}{\\mathop{\\rm arsinh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcosh}{\\mathop{\\rm arcosh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\artanh}{\\mathop{\\rm artanh}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\sech}{\\mathop{\\rm sech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\csch}{\\mathop{\\rm csch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\coth}{\\mathop{\\rm coth}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arsech}{\\mathop{\\rm arsech}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcsch}{\\mathop{\\rm arcsch}\\nolimits}\n\\newcommand{\\arcoth}{\\mathop{\\rm arcoth}\\nolimits}$\n\nIn this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x) = \\sech{x}$ and $v(x) = 4x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot (4x)-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot {(4x)}^{′}}{{(4x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\cdot (4x)-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot 4}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+1)}{4{x}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167341 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c174169-aa47-5034-8eb6-f7f3f6a67204" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+3{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514898} {:answer/id #uuid "4ab17e12-16fb-560a-9043-5efb3ec8c7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515036} {:answer/id #uuid "9e902e56-a500-5a45-80bd-107225b4bc77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515208} {:answer/id #uuid "d88b228f-0bb7-5bcc-ba0a-47bf3064e252" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515329} {:answer/id #uuid "dca96d3f-da77-5807-8f9d-d795652b78cb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-{sech}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e902e56-a500-5a45-80bd-107225b4bc77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515208} :answer-field/id #uuid "49a21963-b209-5ca1-abae-2d86c7c8ded5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165255}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ea9f8f07-a38b-5320-8a01-10ad61981f4b" :question/math-academy-id "q-95282" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x-3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167343 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1dd029f8-246f-53ab-895a-44a2e619c60f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(1+\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514938} {:answer/id #uuid "1e222423-9e1b-5fb3-b014-bcdaac1685b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{sech}⁡x+3x\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514939} {:answer/id #uuid "2435b19c-129f-5f9f-8710-c13e19fa0590" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(1+3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514957} {:answer/id #uuid "ad8d7f77-52a2-5b66-b098-c490722d7e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x(1-3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515237} {:answer/id #uuid "e7525f8b-7814-536f-a1a6-1b6374a6afcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x+\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515358}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ad8d7f77-52a2-5b66-b098-c490722d7e52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x(1-3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515237} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b3b5cbe-0a2f-5765-8344-3c3578534158" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165267}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5cd7acb2-13d4-5813-bdef-217cf5d07814" :question/math-academy-id "q-95285" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=x\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =(x)^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡3x+x\\cdot (\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x)^{′} \\\\  & =1\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡3x+x\\cdot (-3\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\cdot \\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x-3x\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x(1-3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167344 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20dfd53f-f091-567a-8fa9-e79714c620bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x)}{2{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514948} {:answer/id #uuid "4c6863b9-95c4-5271-ab4e-d52585b356dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-2x)}{2{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515041} {:answer/id #uuid "5caa78e3-359d-52e6-94b0-a178afad3b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{2{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515075} {:answer/id #uuid "66dc2572-c7a4-51a1-9206-b481d94d9150" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{{x}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515090} {:answer/id #uuid "bf0b9578-8fb5-5399-bb1d-b58bdf4c5020" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+x)}{{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515279}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5caa78e3-359d-52e6-94b0-a178afad3b15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{2{x}^{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515075} :answer-field/id #uuid "66bb6a07-ca7f-50c9-b79b-cace17e398e0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6a4c419a-8142-571d-8243-5f64958e4a28" :question/math-academy-id "q-95287" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{2{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (2{x}^{2})^{′}}{(2{x}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-4x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{4{x}^{4}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2)}{2{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515545 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fc1200a-020e-579b-aeb4-32e6f6dd2ac7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514904} {:answer/id #uuid "22fc55f5-eece-5862-9495-0d348b157ed8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514954} {:answer/id #uuid "46cb26bc-9466-528b-b53b-aa32a469316e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515021} {:answer/id #uuid "8faee535-6239-5c50-8da1-ab3ca13c3eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515178} {:answer/id #uuid "c42c37da-db11-55f7-a6fa-ee35d397e0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{csch}^{2}⁡x-\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515288}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8faee535-6239-5c50-8da1-ab3ca13c3eed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515178} :answer-field/id #uuid "3fcaf6c9-8a15-52b1-a33f-3f4796a6e58a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515432}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "58b4a157-5f9c-5f77-a21d-1b131c8f0140" :question/math-academy-id "q-95450" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(4\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(-{csch}^{2}⁡x)-(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{csch}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+\\operatorname{coth}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a0450e8-6fb9-5c06-a492-b2d7b234798f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514929} {:answer/id #uuid "43babeff-1414-59a6-a743-e2ee441fdb19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(-\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515016} {:answer/id #uuid "6d949e4f-b4ed-5bc7-9540-4068520fb9fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515100} {:answer/id #uuid "73ac46a2-08ba-5ab9-a955-921da4e67be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515109} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf636ca-0581-5e6c-b5fd-6de80891eeb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515401}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "73ac46a2-08ba-5ab9-a955-921da4e67be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515109} :answer-field/id #uuid "c0a3ff9d-4c25-52f6-a5ce-1978a3171c0c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186165416}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36aad765-1c48-5148-a5cb-bc60296086fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-95451" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)-2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-2(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "291fa27b-e8d1-5ed7-8fbf-082f5be7a7e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514968} {:answer/id #uuid "490d959f-b059-5325-8c05-c4b0cc600f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515030} {:answer/id #uuid "58d6b2ae-f213-5a45-acf0-0b0f01d98283" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515071} {:answer/id #uuid "73b4e303-9008-5e9e-855f-481e71c7524e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515110} {:answer/id #uuid "9c149e2c-33ae-5abe-b943-9a619752febc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{sech}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "490d959f-b059-5325-8c05-c4b0cc600f4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515030} :answer-field/id #uuid "78bb2f4a-9757-595a-a198-758752968458" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b84615c0-35fb-546b-b311-f278e0c613e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-95478" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166761 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "597e3939-e6b4-5237-a16e-8bae92f9b656" :knowledge-point/title "Basic Derivatives of the Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27eb7323-cc8e-5eb9-884b-240fb1bdb83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{sech}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514964} {:answer/id #uuid "28420209-4741-5df8-9bcf-b3d002b845fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514967} {:answer/id #uuid "71c8a2a8-ead0-50d5-ad25-c720628db79b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515105} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7f1c28-26fb-571d-b34a-d848f93d4078" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515272} {:answer/id #uuid "ded027e6-96f7-5da7-a4e2-77b340d6cc09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515340}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28420209-4741-5df8-9bcf-b3d002b845fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6{csch}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514967} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1235ebd-5a71-577a-ad30-6fbc32ad0509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515487}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e0bc8c85-75bd-5d02-9581-c62ed55b672c" :question/math-academy-id "q-95481" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $y=6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we recall the results for the derivatives of the basic reciprocal hyperbolic functions:\n\n$$\n(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)^{′}=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x,\\,(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)^{′}=-{csch}^{2}⁡x\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the given function using these results, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(6\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =6(-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =-6{csch}^{2}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515555 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "000ac2db-823f-5c0a-b07e-bb2931ec4a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514871} {:answer/id #uuid "0b9e21a4-7a29-56e5-b72e-0fdff889f662" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{sech}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514897} {:answer/id #uuid "bb7be486-4971-575d-b870-4310be3f5e35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sech}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515269} {:answer/id #uuid "d3a28112-e00d-5d59-939f-1f4609fb499d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515316} {:answer/id #uuid "fb8f51dd-25a7-51e7-9f0d-a86386cfddb2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{tanh}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "000ac2db-823f-5c0a-b07e-bb2931ec4a29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514871} :answer-field/id #uuid "49f4380a-e4c2-512c-bf58-08136b8a4df3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515435}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6866b59d-bbba-56df-8e9c-26cc543fc023" :question/math-academy-id "q-95566" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g,\\,g=1-4x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-4.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =2\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g \\\\  & =-8\\operatorname{csch}⁡(1-4x)\\operatorname{coth}⁡(1-4x).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515553 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01b6c708-c1e5-5ee0-b136-0843073b4ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514875} {:answer/id #uuid "20318a3b-cddf-5f49-a770-aa54022d9211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514945} {:answer/id #uuid "2ba9842f-6d92-5b98-9e66-644e6c2d1a4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\operatorname{csch}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514970} {:answer/id #uuid "93151f0c-21d4-5e36-9952-db632486e2a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12{tanh}^{2}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515182} {:answer/id #uuid "fdd64067-8043-5950-a2a1-3a7b7fdce288" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{csch}^{2}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "20318a3b-cddf-5f49-a770-aa54022d9211" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514945} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9230a28-06b0-581f-81e1-12ba5c6ce005" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515477}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6703e5b6-66a0-5cda-938a-ed7160c9206e" :question/math-academy-id "q-95568" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=4\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g,\\,g=3x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-4\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡g\\operatorname{tanh}⁡g \\\\  & =-12\\operatorname{sech}⁡3x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515540 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58eb1a2f-da58-55f3-8568-74f50a7918a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515073} {:answer/id #uuid "81b12827-b2c6-5675-8386-55a92b9f0a33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515139} {:answer/id #uuid "9f37f12b-a6ff-5b18-8085-e0b9d1178fa0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515210} {:answer/id #uuid "adc65e90-ae5d-5e28-b418-5de7054b3a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515238} {:answer/id #uuid "e88cd52a-ff88-5f62-99a9-073b12b25a57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{coth}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515362}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58eb1a2f-da58-55f3-8568-74f50a7918a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515073} :answer-field/id #uuid "a73eab0e-5052-533a-9a91-63a4d2681994" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515476}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "51513d5e-ca42-5754-a902-1af12bc25041" :question/math-academy-id "q-95569" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=-\\operatorname{csch}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡g\\operatorname{coth}⁡g \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e61680f-34d0-54c9-a581-fc46337f2489" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x{sech}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515045} {:answer/id #uuid "c2870e74-3428-5720-b294-4aedf55aa1a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515285} {:answer/id #uuid "c853cba8-3165-56c6-a436-2b32f112bafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515297} {:answer/id #uuid "d5214c15-24d4-5045-a3fa-cdf23f818462" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-x{csch}^{2}⁡2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515319} {:answer/id #uuid "e6496d12-4f39-58a0-bc57-cd3eaaeb3ece" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡({x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c853cba8-3165-56c6-a436-2b32f112bafb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515297} :answer-field/id #uuid "fdada9a0-319d-50fa-a0c4-8211688157c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "76beb3b0-dbd8-5192-b70b-0a4bac401337" :question/math-academy-id "q-95570" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡({x}^{2}-1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\operatorname{coth}⁡g,\\,g={x}^{2}-1\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=-{csch}^{2}⁡g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-{csch}^{2}⁡g\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡g \\\\  & =-2x{csch}^{2}⁡({x}^{2}-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515591 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166762 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6fd03e86-fab7-5157-b0f3-62c522dc212c" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Chain Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61276995-74bd-5344-aa45-015217ab0d57" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515081} {:answer/id #uuid "6bd2715d-56f1-531c-9661-a9c48c9057cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515096} {:answer/id #uuid "78513305-089d-5926-bd36-dc21c4328d46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x{tanh}^{2}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515121} {:answer/id #uuid "8b54fd43-f7d2-592e-902d-5621425e00b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515163} {:answer/id #uuid "e944c330-fa87-5fb5-b030-527351a8f08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{sech}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515364}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8b54fd43-f7d2-592e-902d-5621425e00b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515163} :answer-field/id #uuid "33fef8da-1fed-575c-b52c-5735f185e8df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515428}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b9b1e144-f837-55bf-a0c3-8113231511af" :question/math-academy-id "q-95577" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{sech}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=2{g}^{2},\\,g=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}=4g,\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the two results together and substituting for $g$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =4g(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x) \\\\  & =-4{sech}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515518 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d162b6f-3bb5-573d-9a18-2c860b4368a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2+x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514900} {:answer/id #uuid "197fd5ad-27fa-5f37-82bd-6030ed45adaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514928} {:answer/id #uuid "43fa1256-5bed-59ec-868b-cad71abb11e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515019} {:answer/id #uuid "85b20bf6-ba1e-536c-9760-343ba5f356c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2-x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515150} {:answer/id #uuid "b9aedc43-fe07-5c3a-8a28-1ba22a9c08b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515267}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "43fa1256-5bed-59ec-868b-cad71abb11e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515019} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f3fe267-45dc-5a4c-8818-eeaf17174ee4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515420}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05fabaa5-d0f1-544a-aecb-26138b15f8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-95580" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x,$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot g(x).$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x)}^{′} \\\\  & =2x\\cdot \\operatorname{csch}⁡4x+{x}^{2}\\cdot (-4\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x-4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{csch}⁡4x\\cdot {{(1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x)}_{⏟}}_{g(x)}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=1-2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡4x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18df1be8-527c-5a6e-9f98-b10d18413d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514927} {:answer/id #uuid "2d38c782-b76b-5f2e-9bc1-52a75a14aae8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}(1-2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sech}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514972} {:answer/id #uuid "5df3b1cb-49c5-5619-b74d-771d324baa71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}(1+2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{csch}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515078} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e88966-4166-5138-ba39-d7f1856ad0b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515217} {:answer/id #uuid "d89ce40e-349e-5c17-89d4-b56369e8b9c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡2x-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡2x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "18df1be8-527c-5a6e-9f98-b10d18413d0c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514927} :answer-field/id #uuid "c01224a1-e3b1-57d5-aa15-96438779d2bf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515486}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7b044358-869c-54b8-ba0e-868b6f91f848" :question/math-academy-id "q-95581" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2})}^{′} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}+2x\\cdot (-2x{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2} \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{coth}⁡{x}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{csch}^{2}⁡{x}^{2})\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515547 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47c6288c-a7a5-5339-b54b-1574f3d6b867" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6x(2\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515024} {:answer/id #uuid "6cf54fd4-6b0f-50ff-a220-778bd198efc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515097} {:answer/id #uuid "8a431668-bf6d-5679-ae3b-f87922954d7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515159} {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c404c-45ca-5797-a6b2-587a4722a97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515280} {:answer/id #uuid "f1c2ee11-1fdd-5116-b3c9-c3625f9cb203" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2x(2\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+{x}^{2}{sech}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515379}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bf9c404c-45ca-5797-a6b2-587a4722a97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515280} :answer-field/id #uuid "ee35a739-301f-5040-bed9-e710c7640e85" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515509}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "598d9b4b-1def-5b7e-8724-7abe41dc985d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95585" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=2{x}^{3}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=2{x}^{3}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{coth}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(2{x}^{3})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{coth}⁡x+2{x}^{3}\\cdot (-{csch}^{2}⁡x) \\\\  & =6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-2{x}^{3}{csch}^{2}⁡x \\\\  & =2{x}^{2}(3\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-x{csch}^{2}⁡x)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515601 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166763 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a991a2f4-b96a-5f92-8b52-6102647be98e" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Product Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14996826-58fd-5f33-872c-ee218d66b803" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x{coth}^{2}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514916} {:answer/id #uuid "2079f812-1687-58bc-84c8-a6540751137c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514946} {:answer/id #uuid "544fd53c-bf80-59a4-b498-861dbea14ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515059} {:answer/id #uuid "79f1e788-3c2d-59d8-a0bf-2ec512ab473a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(2x{coth}^{2}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515126} {:answer/id #uuid "c46b8049-5168-58e4-97c5-3a3c60907ffc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x+2x{coth}^{2}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "544fd53c-bf80-59a4-b498-861dbea14ecf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515059} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a955475-a532-56de-a95a-903c6b5439c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ca80da50-025a-555f-9c99-42892fcfd87d" :question/math-academy-id "q-95588" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=-3x{csch}^{2}⁡x.$" :question/worked-solution "Here, we have the product of two functions $u(x)=-3x$ and $v(x)={csch}^{2}⁡x.$ So, we apply the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={(-3x)}^{′}\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x+(-3x)\\cdot {({csch}^{2}⁡x)}^{′} \\\\  & =-3\\cdot {csch}^{2}⁡x-3x\\cdot (2\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x) \\\\  & =-3{csch}^{2}⁡x+6x{csch}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x \\\\  & =3{csch}^{2}⁡x(2x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515575 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3017d4ed-3882-520b-a996-9fdf270542a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x+x{tanh}^{2}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514980} {:answer/id #uuid "59f86a6e-f337-50e8-81fb-3fddff5be091" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2{x}^{2}{tanh}^{2}⁡2x}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515074} {:answer/id #uuid "759f1f90-6344-577e-9bac-c36fc6f545db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(1-x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515114} {:answer/id #uuid "aa2b53d9-b9f2-5c4b-a6ff-2d9c5e028405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515230} {:answer/id #uuid "b5fb8197-f137-5a59-878a-191936644f84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-x{tanh}^{2}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515256}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa2b53d9-b9f2-5c4b-a6ff-2d9c5e028405" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515230} :answer-field/id #uuid "9407eea0-1e45-5270-a47d-8ad06eaf5ea2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515465}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9031fff8-a36e-5cc9-9588-e90f1f428aa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-95889" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{({x}^{2})}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x-{x}^{2}(-2\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{{sech}^{2}⁡2x} \\\\  & =\\frac{2x(1+x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡2x)}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡2x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515569 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "049fa100-40fb-558d-a706-98cb51270374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514883} {:answer/id #uuid "8548fcd7-b1dc-55d8-b576-44ec1a1cb5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515148} {:answer/id #uuid "9bbb7054-2e28-56a6-ac8b-4a4516f8e59f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515201} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a6cb95-2d20-5064-94c1-f104d506b1ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515350} {:answer/id #uuid "eafd044b-db1b-5753-972f-0c09ea3f5918" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{coth}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515368}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8548fcd7-b1dc-55d8-b576-44ec1a1cb5a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515148} :answer-field/id #uuid "20a0d20a-e247-5de6-9e87-dc2aa68c5128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515422}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8386701e-f444-5c82-8928-9b7b2e5dd7d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-95892" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{sech}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡x-\\operatorname{sech}⁡x\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}{{sin}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overset{g(x)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)}}}{{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515559 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a4049a-fca7-5f52-bfb1-771580341b24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514910} {:answer/id #uuid "15ccd49d-999f-5394-bd85-dc0b8b867ba4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514919} {:answer/id #uuid "2bd04e6e-2a4a-5265-b550-0dcfb916da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} {:answer/id #uuid "4ace196d-01ef-57ff-8b7f-750161ecd9d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515038} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e6f4e6-23c8-5da2-a89b-5234a110c448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515383}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2bd04e6e-2a4a-5265-b550-0dcfb916da3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514971} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e3c01d9-f6b5-59af-9a9b-7d7b991856a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515469}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6cac54f6-b1ee-5704-8eb2-39e7e0d78de0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95893" :question/problem "$$\n\nIf $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x},$ then ${f}^{′}(x)=-\\frac{g(x)}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}.$ What is $g(x)?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{′}}{{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot (\\frac{1}{x})}{{ln}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\overset{g(x)}{\\overset{⏞}{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1)}}}{x{ln}^{2}⁡x}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $g(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(x\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+1).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515605 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166764 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "08d9798e-a4bb-5f04-9d49-494990c52bff" :knowledge-point/title "Differentiating Reciprocal Hyperbolic Functions Using the Quotient Rule"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ed2e2e3-518c-5e68-89da-39c8b1b16487" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514941} {:answer/id #uuid "8fc61f6c-7f69-5a3e-891d-3c81503f21cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{tanh}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515179} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c18b32-dba8-5ee5-97c1-1e43053d9290" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515224} {:answer/id #uuid "d9760669-aa3f-50da-81bb-626fffa1ca8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515331} {:answer/id #uuid "fdb45133-c88a-50de-a15e-f261ed67b159" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{sech}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515406}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d9760669-aa3f-50da-81bb-626fffa1ca8b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515331} :answer-field/id #uuid "e02ecce8-68a0-5491-9b9a-ae26b78a95e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515502}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d2bf0ce7-0ebf-56f9-bf0e-f167e2403753" :question/math-academy-id "q-95896" :question/problem "$$\n\nFind the derivative of $f(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x}{{3}^{x}}.$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)=\\operatorname{csch}⁡x$ and $v(x)={3}^{x}.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{(\\operatorname{csch}⁡x)}^{′}\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot {({3}^{x})}^{′}}{{({3}^{x})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\operatorname{coth}⁡x)\\cdot {3}^{x}-\\operatorname{csch}⁡x\\cdot ({3}^{x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{{3}^{x}\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{2x}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\operatorname{csch}⁡x(\\operatorname{coth}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)}{{3}^{x}}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
